        {
            "text": "Anne Innis Dagg\nNew!\nIn 1956, Dr. Anne Innis Dagg became the first Western researcher to study any mammal in the wild in Africa. She is still known as one of the foremost experts on giraffes.",
            "href": "https://www.historicacanada.ca/productions/minutes/anne-innis-dagg"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mary Riter Hamilton\nStaff Pick\nMary Riter Hamilton painted the battlefields after the First World War as a testament to its devastating cost. She would suffer mental and physical illnesses as a result of documenting the experiences of Canadian soldiers.",
            "href": "https://www.historicacanada.ca/productions/minutes/heritage-minutes-mary-riter-hamilton"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bora Laskin\nPopular\nOne of Canada’s greatest legal scholars, Bora Laskin overcame antisemitism to become the first Jewish Chief Justice of the Supreme Court of Canada.",
            "href": "https://www.historicacanada.ca/productions/minutes/bora-laskin"
        },
